	(text_box "Place the TMP119 physically close to the flash storage chip ideally within a few millimeters on the same PCB side. \nAvoide thermal vias directly under the TMP119. Use a solid copper reference plane to allow the sensor to track the flash package temperature rather than localized PCB heating.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 65.532 164.592 0)
		(size 52.832 16.2161)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "daf1c0b6-9383-454e-96a0-7c4f574efb12")
	)
	(text_box "INA226 Shunt and VBUS Connection Options - Design Note\n\nThis design uses the INA226 to measure current and power on USB VBUS rails via a series shunt resistor. The INA226 has two different measurement inputs that must be understood separately.\n\nShont Measurement (VIN+ and VIN-)\n\nThe shunt resistor is always placed in series with the rall being monitored.\n\n1)VIN+ connects to the upstream side of the shunt (closer to the source or connector)\n2)VIN- connects to the downstream side of the shunt (closer to the load)\n\nThis connection determines the direction and magnitude of the measured current and must not be changed.\n\nBos Voltage Measurement (VBUS)\n\nVBUS is a single ended voltage sense input referenced to GND. It does not power the device. VBUS can be connected to different points depending \non what voltage and power meaning is desired.\n\nOption A - VBUS = VIN- (Load Side Voltage)\nVBUS tied to VIN- measures the voltage delivered to the circuit after the shunt.\nReported power represents power actually delivered to the downstream load.\nThis is the recommended and implemented option in this design.\n\nOption B - VBUS = VIN+ (Source Side Voltage)\nVBUS tied to VIN+ measures the source of connector voltage before the shunt.\nReported power represents power drawn from the source, including shunt losses.\nTnis may be preferred when characterising USB port loading"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.78 60.1888 0)
		(size 136.144 65.2872)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e76f5fe3-6e83-489e-888c-f3165b715e73")
	)
